Lepton: build FFmpeg for x86_64 without its Vulkan support

WayDroid-ATV's FFmpeg 7.1 Android configuration enables Vulkan on x86 and
x86_64 (hwcontext, Vulkan encoders and hwaccels). Android 14's Vulkan
headers predate VK_KHR_video_decode_av1, so libavutil/hwcontext_vulkan.c
fails to compile (undeclared VK_KHR_VIDEO_DECODE_AV1_EXTENSION_NAME).
Lepton's video decoding uses VA-API, and the ARM configurations already
build without Vulkan.

Turn off every Vulkan CONFIG_ switch in the x86_64 configuration (make
fragment, C header and assembler header), the Vulkan hwaccels and encoders
in the x86_64 section of config_components.h, and drop the two Vulkan
encoders from the x86_64 codec list; otherwise libavcodec.so fails to link
(undefined ff_*_vulkan_hwaccel and ff_*_vulkan_encoder).

diff --git a/android/config-x86_64-x86_64.mak b/android/config-x86_64-x86_64.mak
--- a/android/config-x86_64-x86_64.mak
+++ b/android/config-x86_64-x86_64.mak
@@ -626,7 +626,7 @@ CONFIG_LIBDRM=yes
 CONFIG_VAAPI=yes
 !CONFIG_VDPAU=yes
 !CONFIG_VIDEOTOOLBOX=yes
-CONFIG_VULKAN=yes
+!CONFIG_VULKAN=yes
 CONFIG_V4L2_M2M=yes
 !CONFIG_FTRAPV=yes
 !CONFIG_GRAY=yes
@@ -789,7 +789,7 @@ CONFIG_VIDEODSP=yes
 CONFIG_VP3DSP=yes
 CONFIG_VP56DSP=yes
 CONFIG_VP8DSP=yes
-CONFIG_VULKAN_ENCODE=yes
+!CONFIG_VULKAN_ENCODE=yes
 CONFIG_WMA_FREQS=yes
 CONFIG_WMV2DSP=yes
 CONFIG_AAC_ADTSTOASC_BSF=yes
@@ -1653,7 +1653,7 @@ CONFIG_H263_V4L2M2M_ENCODER=yes
 CONFIG_H264_V4L2M2M_ENCODER=yes
 CONFIG_H264_VAAPI_ENCODER=yes
 !CONFIG_H264_VIDEOTOOLBOX_ENCODER=yes
-CONFIG_H264_VULKAN_ENCODER=yes
+!CONFIG_H264_VULKAN_ENCODER=yes
 !CONFIG_HEVC_AMF_ENCODER=yes
 !CONFIG_HEVC_D3D12VA_ENCODER=yes
 !CONFIG_HEVC_MEDIACODEC_ENCODER=yes
@@ -1663,7 +1663,7 @@ CONFIG_H264_VULKAN_ENCODER=yes
 CONFIG_HEVC_V4L2M2M_ENCODER=yes
 !CONFIG_HEVC_VAAPI_ENCODER=yes
 !CONFIG_HEVC_VIDEOTOOLBOX_ENCODER=yes
-CONFIG_HEVC_VULKAN_ENCODER=yes
+!CONFIG_HEVC_VULKAN_ENCODER=yes
 !CONFIG_LIBKVAZAAR_ENCODER=yes
 !CONFIG_MJPEG_QSV_ENCODER=yes
